crystalize packages a Ruby (Rails) application, taken from a git branch,
into a single executable: Crystal launcher, relocatable Ruby, gems and the
application code precompiled to YARV bytecode. Secrets stay outside the
binary (age-encrypted YAML), so does the database; Active Storage files
are kept clear or encrypted on disk.

`crystalize port` writes a FreeBSD port of the application, built by
poudriere from public distfiles (Ruby, gems) and from the private
application sources fetched on the builder before the bulk.
